   border. That line lands exactly on our card's top border and paints over it,
   so the card's top edge — including the hover highlight — reads as missing
   while the other three sides keep their color. Our rows are self-bordered
   cards, so the divider is dropped. Note the ancestor order: Obsidian's
   `.setting-group` wraps the plugin root (`.setting-group > .setting-items >
   .setting-item.opencodian-settings-direct-host > .opencodian-settings`), so the
   selector has to hang off `.opencodian-settings` the same way the row-card rule
